  "body": "**Stacked on #566** (#561, locate the part in a fixture). It includes #566's commits until that PR merges.\n\n## What changed\nTurning a part on the Model page rotated its stock rigidly with it (`move_model.rs`), so a square blank came out tilted. #566 fixed this for locate only. Now every `MoveModel` that **turns** the part uses the same square-stock rule (`stock_follow::keep_square`):\n- **Square stocks:** a box or cylinder whose axes lie along the setup's axes (any quarter turn) keeps its orientation. It is refitted around the part's new place, keeping each side's allowance, measured in the stock's own frame before the move.\n- **Quarter turns refit too; the block doesn't rotate with the part.** One rule for one gesture, so 89.99° and 90° give the same kind of blank. Top stays top, so a \"+top for facing\" allowance never moves onto a side. A yaw quarter turn refits to the same size anyway.\n- **Unchanged cases:**\n  - Translation-only moves keep the old rigid carry, with no refit and no mesh rebuild.\n  - A copied-from-model stock, or one already off the axes, still turns rigidly with the part.\n- **Locate:** `MoveModel::locating` now just calls `MoveModel::new`.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/571-movemodel-square-stock.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **Updated pin:** `commands_undo::moving_one_part_carries_existing_stock_and_undo_restores_both` keeps its intent (the stock follows, undo restores both). After a 90° yaw plus a move, the stock stays square and wraps the part.\n- **New `move_model_stock`:**\n  - a 30° turn keeps a box stock square with each allowance, and undo/redo are exact;\n  - a 30° turn keeps a cylinder upright;\n  - translation-only moves carry the stock rigidly as before;\n  - a turned or copied stock still turns rigidly.\n  - The pin and both 30° tests failed before the change.\n- **Gate:** app lib (105), commands_undo, fixture_locate(_stock), setup_align, plane_align(_edges), top_stock, setup_stock_source, stock_stamp, project_roundtrip, wcs_align, pick_doors, stock_view, stock_play, the ui models tests and the ui locate tests pass. Clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nA hands-on GUI turn on the Model page.\n\nChangelog: Turning a part on the Model page keeps a square box or cylinder stock square to the machine, refitted around the part with its per-side allowances; moves that only slide the part carry the stock as before (#571)\n\nFixes #571\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
